# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you need.
# `.env.local` (and `.env`) are gitignored; never commit real secrets.
#
# NOTE: BYOK (bring-your-own-key) needs NONE of this. Pasting a key into the
# Insights tab stores it in expo-secure-store on the device and sends it only to
# the provider. This file is only for the OPTIONAL hosted-proxy mode.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side (inlined into the app bundle — never put secrets here).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute URL of a proxy endpoint that YOU host. It is only used when no key
# is stored on the device. It must accept { "notes": [{ id, text, createdAt }] }
# and return a WellbeingInsight. Leave unset for BYOK-only use.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_INSIGHTS_API_URL=https://your-server.example.com/insights

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted server only (not read by this app).
#
# The repo ships no server route, so these are only relevant if you build your
# own proxy. Do NOT prefix them with EXPO_PUBLIC_ — that would inline them into
# the client bundle and expose the key. The shared modules in src/lib
# (insights-core.ts, ai-providers.ts) can be reused in such a server.
#
# GROQ_API_KEY=            # https://console.groq.com/keys  (free)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=          # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  (free)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# INSIGHTS_PROVIDER=groq   # groq | gemini | openai | anthropic
# INSIGHTS_MODEL=          # override the model
# INSIGHTS_BASE_URL=       # override the base URL
# INSIGHTS_API_KEY=        # generic key, used before the provider-specific one
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
